# MFE Believer 1960, current design: 2x20 cm root wing inserts, Starlink Mini on top, 6S5P, 5.9 kg.
# For ArduPilot SITL's built-in plane model (--model plane:believer.json).
# Needs the local SIM_Plane patch (patches/ardupilot-sitl-plane-electric-propulsion.patch):
# "mass", "inertia" and the motor/propeller/battery keys below do not exist upstream.
# Original 5.0 kg design: believer_5kg.json.
#
# Airframe:
#   wing 1.96 m + 2x0.20 m EPO inserts at the root (assumed 0.30 m chord): s 0.634 m^2, b 2.36 m,
#   c 0.269 m (s / b), AR 8.78. mass 5.9 kg: 2.2 airframe + 2.2 6S5P + 0.3 payload + 1.1 Starlink
#   + ~0.1 inserts. Design maximum set by the user; the extended spar has not been load-tested.
#   inertia [0.55, 0.22, 0.77] kg m^2: estimate (wing 0.8 kg over the span, motor pods 0.25 kg each at
#   0.55 m, Starlink 1.1 kg ~0.10 m above the CG), not measured.
# Lift:  c_lift_a 5.118 /rad = 2*pi*AR/(AR+2); c_lift_0 0.25 (assumed incidence); alpha_stall 0.25
#        gives CLmax 1.15, a clean stall of about 11.4 m/s at 5.9 kg.
# Drag:  oswald 0.8 (assumed). c_drag_p 0.0348 on the new area: the original airframe's
#        0.514 m^2 x 0.0327 (fitted to the forum Believer flight), 0.12 m^2 of added wing at 0.010, and
#        the Starlink dish on top as 1.0 N at 20 m/s (assumed; a fairing would reduce it).
# Propulsion: 2x SunnySky X3120 585KV (43.5 mOhm listed, 1.0 A no-load assumed), ESC 95%,
#        APC 11x7E with Ct and Cp fitted as quadratics in J to APC's PER3_11x7E.dat.
#        Battery 6S5P P50B: SIM_BATT_VOLTAGE 25.2, SIM_BATT_CAP_AH 25, 22 mOhm pack + wiring.
#        The battery feeds propulsion only: Starlink (25-40 W) and avionics are not drawn from it.
# Launch: rubber catapult, 3.3 g over a ~3.8 m stroke (~15 m/s on a rail): launch_accel 32.4 m/s^2 for
#        launch_time 0.48 s along body x (IMU 3.4 g peak). Was 59 m/s^2 for 0.39 s, which logged 6.3 g:
#        too rough for the EPO airframe (compare/launch.md). Fired by servo 7 > 1700. SITL launches level
#        along the ground with belly friction, not from an inclined rail. The launch keys need the local patch.
# Stability and control derivatives are SITL's defaults (skywalker_2013), unchanged.

{
